nergy\\\",\\\"comparison\\\":\\\"gte\\\",\\\"value\\\":10}}],\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"interrupts\\\":[],\\\"notes\\\":[\\\"The meeting coordinate is distinct from Moss's last observed position; their movement may affect whether an exchange is possible.\\\",\\\"Offer only the measured pressure finding, not a claim about nutrition, toxicity, or general material strength.\\\",\\\"Learning cultivation does not establish that any particular unit will root.\\\"],\\\"preferences\\\":[\\\"Preserve known-safe berries for meals rather than eating unverified hazelnuts.\\\",\\\"Prefer independent exploration with voluntary exchanges of actual findings.\\\"],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"local-foods\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Which nearby foods can safely support an independent life?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Known berry nutrition is 8 with zero toxicity.\\\",\\\"At tick 25 inventory contains five berries and 1.9 hazelnuts.\\\",\\\"The tick-25 pressure trial at load 0.2 reported held=true and flexibility=0, consuming 0.1 hazelnut.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"Hazelnut nutrition, toxicity and processing requirements remain unknown; the pressure result does not establish edibility.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Maintain a practical safe-food reserve and investigate another local food.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[\\\"Gathered and eaten known-safe berries.\\\",\\\"Observed the hazelnut plant and an owned sample.\\\",\\\"Performed one small non-ingestive pressure trial.\\\"],\\\"outputs\\\":[\\\"Known-safe berry reserve.\\\",\\\"Remaining hazelnut sample.\\\",\\\"One measured hazelnut pressure response.\\\"],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"Evidence supporting hazelnut food use and a suitable method to obtain it safely.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Share the measured result with Moss and learn the available cultivation method without assuming establishment.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"The berry reserve provides an alternative to ingesting unv